{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he called.</b> Moses, or the reader." "<b>Massah and Merivah.</b> Because of two things that are mentioned, and the rule of the sacred language is that whenever two things are mentioned, it always begins from the second, which is the closer one, as in \"and I gave to Isaac Jacob and Esau\" (Joshua 24:4), and afterward \"and I gave to Esau\" (there), and so too here he mentioned first Massah, and after it Merivah, then returned to explain the naming of Merivah on account of the quarrel of the children of Israel with Moses, and explained Massah on account of their testing YHWH — and behold, he explained Massah as \"Is YHWH among us,\" that He should provide all our needs, and this second group provoked YHWH more than the first, therefore he said: \"You shall not test YHWH your Elohim, as you tested at Massah\" (Deuteronomy 6:16)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:21.518283762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}